      "writtenOn": "2020-10-20T16:54:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Comment: Done.\n\nI added essentially symmetrical code for the data role for cable plug traffic. I didn\u0027t do anything for the conditions before an explicit contract is in place, because I don\u0027t think there\u0027s anything we can do at that point to remedy them, and I don\u0027t think the pe_attempt_port_discovery will run at that time anyway.\n\nI\u0027m not sure if you also wanted me to try to fix the data role before giving up on SOP discovery in PD 2.0. I think that has some symmetry arguments in its favor, but it could bear to be its own CL.\n\nI note that the role swap logic in pe_attempt_port_discovery purports to be a policy decision. With the addition of on-demand VCONN Swaps, we still technically have a policy of trying to become VCONN Source once before discovery, but it isn\u0027t really an important policy. It could be removed without a practical change in behavior. Conceivably, we could get to the point where the same is true WRT data role. In any case, putting this logic in the discovery function seems a bit arbitrary at this point. The real policy decision is setting the flags at startup, and maybe those should just be checked in the ready states.\n\nHow far do you want me to go with this?",
      "parentUuid": "756dce8c_53a49619",
      "revId": "96aa008ed83890dd4241f3d93a4c9154bea31833",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64b5fde9_62d23788",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4768,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-20T17:13:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, before a contract there\u0027s definitely nothing we can/should be doing if we\u0027re not source.\n\nI was mostly wondering if we should either similarly mark SOP discovery FAILED when we\u0027re a PD 2.0 UFP, or if we should leave SOP\u0027 as NEEDED in that case (though then we\u0027d transition in and out of the discovery states a lot for SOP\u0027)\n\nAll the swaps (vconn, data, power, etc.) need to start moving into the DPM for our per-port policy driver. I have this on my own TODO list after finishing up the currently spec\u0027d notifications for the AP, so you don\u0027t need to take it any further than you\u0027d like to.",
      "parentUuid": "cf480cd9_16c084df",
      "revId": "96aa008ed83890dd4241f3d93a4c9154bea31833",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a720a65_7a3355af",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4768,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-20T17:33:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WRT failing out of SOP discovery if we don\u0027t have the right roles, because that will produce a more obviously final discovery result for the AP to consume. I think that can wait for another CL, though.\n\nWRT swapping by policy from the DPM, that makes sense at a high level. Given the VCONN contention that the spec seems to naturally invite, I think it makes a fair amount of sense for the PE to have logic to try to become VCONN Source on its own, at least during discovery. I think this kind of trading back and forth is less likely for data role, so it would make more sense to just try once to become our preferred role and set the preference by policy.\n\nDo you think I should back out my patchset to try to become DFP before communicating with the cable plug in 2.0?",
      "parentUuid": "64b5fde9_62d23788",
      "revId": "96aa008ed83890dd4241f3d93a4c9154bea31833",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
